     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">I&#39;m hoping someone will point me in a direction or at least opine in brief.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">I\r\n know R reasonably well, but not much else, programming/ networking-wise.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><b><br></b></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><b><u>The problem:</u></b></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">I have a firm that owns remote devices which near-constantly stream raw data via HTTP POSTs of xml or json.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">I want to capture and store this data automatically, to later analyze and monitor it through a shiny dashboard.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><b><u>My plan:</u></b><br>1- set up virtual machine (&quot;VM&quot;) running CentOS<br>2- install R and MariaDB<br>3- use Gunicorn as a server to listen for POSTs<br>4- automatically parse and save the XML to MariaDB using python<br>5- Using a cron job, have the VM email periodic reports generated by RMarkdown/R on the VM<br>6- Have an app hosted on my <a href=\"http://shinayapp.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinayapp.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362084549000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2gG7inBufVq5AibCunHSmi\">shinayapp.io</a> account connect to the vm db to get the data at launch (with dplyr)</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">I&#39;ve done <a href=\"https://support.rstudio.com/hc/requests/1\" rel=\"ticket nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://support.rstudio.com/hc/requests/1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362084549000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2P7SppT71JQ-_HxgNFWooz\">#1</a>-2 above, and feel confident I can do <a href=\"https://support.rstudio.com/hc/requests/5\" rel=\"ticket nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://support.rstudio.com/hc/requests/5&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362084549000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Gft540kXHja4JzpKU6JYQ\">#5</a>-6.  Steps 3 and 4 are more difficult.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><b><u>My questions:</u></b><br>-\r\n Is the above a reasonable structure?  It strikes me as overly complex, \r\nand I&#39;m wondering if there&#39;s an R solution to eliminate the python \r\nand/or Gunicorn steps.</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">-\r\n my data is almost always rectangular, but very long.  Should I consider\r\n skipping the read/write to maria in favor of just writing to csv&#39;s (or \r\nthe new Feather)?</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">-\r\n given that I&#39;m setting up a VM, should I just set up shiny server open \r\nsource on the VM, or is this level of knowledge overhead considerably \r\nhigher?</p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\"><br></p><p style=\"color:rgb(43,46,47);font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Verdana,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22px\" dir=\"auto\">Thanks for any guidance</p></div>"
